  "type": "spr",
  "stimulus": null,
  "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In a sample, <math alttext=\"80 percent sign\"><mn>80</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the items are faulty. There are <math alttext=\"88\"><mn>88</mn>\n</math> faulty items in the sample. How many total items are in the sample?</p>",
  "answerOptions": [],
  "keys": [
    "110"
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "110"
  ],
  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"110\"><mn>110</mn>\n</math>. Let <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represent the total number of items in the sample. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext=\"80 percent sign\"><mn>80</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the items are faulty and that there are <math alttext=\"88\"><mn>88</mn>\n</math> faulty items in the sample. Therefore, <math alttext=\"80 percent sign\"><mn>80</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"88\"><mn>88</mn>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"80 percent sign\"><mn>80</mn><mo>%</mo></math> can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"StartFraction 80 Over 100 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>80</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math>, it follows that <math alttext=\"StartFraction 80 Over 100 EndFraction x equals 88\"><mfrac><mn>80</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>88</mn></math>.&nbsp;Multiplying both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"80 x equals 8,800\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>80</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>8,800</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"80\"><mn>80</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals 110\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>110</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, there are <math alttext=\"110\"><mn>110</mn>\n</math> total items in the sample.</p>",
